   "MatterHistoryActionName": "elected",
   "MatterHistoryActionText": "The Rules, Confirmations, and Public Elections Committee recommended the nominees. The President called for an election to fill one vacancy on the Health and Educational Facilities Board. Nominations previously made were Matt Wiltshire, Dr. Ouida Davis, Keith Randall, and Howard Jones. The following vote was taken on the nominated candidates: Matt Wiltshire (21): Evans-Segall, Allen, Hill, Cortese, Parker, Capp, Benedict, Hancock, Webb, Evans, Bradford, Huffman, Gregg, Cash, Druffel, Johnston, Nash, Benton, Rutherford, Ewing, and Spain; Dr. Ouida Davis (12): Suara, Porterfield, Kimbrough, Toombs, Gamble, Harrell, Vo, Preptit, Ellis, Sepulveda, Styles, and Lee; Howard Jones (1): Eslick; Keith Randall (0); Abstain (0). The president declared that Matt Wiltshire was elected to the Board.",
